      <title>China's AI Agents Are Trapped</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-11-05/china-s-ai-agents-are-trapped</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">a0170bdd744ec08d0607dad7</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 18:00:18 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Earlier this year, scenes of retirees and young people waiting in long lines to install the AI agent OpenClaw went viral in China. Even as the government warned of cybersecurity risks, consumers rushed to try the long-hyped Next Big Thing in artificial intelligence: tools that don’t just chat, but act on their own.</description>
